   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.2",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.2\n\n**What it does:** a new picture in the shape of your photo. MoGe 3 reads the photo's 3D shape (pose, framing), the control LoRA follows that map, your prompt decides everything else. No map to prepare. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Photo**: the picture whose shape you want. The result gets its shape at about 1 megapixel.\n   - **Prompt**: describe the new picture. The saved prompt is written for `example.png` (the drawing that ships with ComfyUI).\n   - **Follow the shape until** 0.6: the map guides the first 0.6 of the run, then the model finishes freely (template). 1 = follow it the whole way.\n   - **Steps** 25, **CFG** 3: the template's. **Seed**: fixed; new number = new picture.\n2. **Models**: five files, see the Downloads note.\n3. **Photo → shape map**: the map node is set to *depth* (template). *mask* keeps only the outline (looser): switch to it when the result copies the photo too closely. This switch is in group 3 on purpose, so App mode does not show it: open group 3 to change it. The preview shows the map.\n4. **Prompt + shape**: nothing to change.\n5. **Sampling**: ER-SDE / simple, shift 5, Skip Layer Guidance on block 24 (all from the template).\n6. **Run**. The result is saved to `output/MOSS-Image/`; the slider node shows map and result.\n\n**What to expect:** The photo's shape at about 1 MP (768x1360 for a 9:16 photo), 32 to 33 s on the lab's 24 GB card in a 10 GiB budget. Pose and framing followed the photo in all tests (example.png, the full-body photo).\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3 on the lab server (RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB), --reserve-vram 13.5 --disable-dynamic-vram, no custom nodes. Not run on a 12 GB card yet.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -800,
